menu "PixelClip display (RM67162 AMOLED)"

    config HAIRCLIP_LCD_PCLK_MHZ
        int "AMOLED QSPI clock (MHz)"
        range 10 80
        default 40
        help
            QSPI clock for the RM67162 panel. 40 MHz is what the Waveshare demo uses and is
            verified on this board; 80 MHz roughly halves flush time but is untested.

    config HAIRCLIP_LCD_BOUNCE_ROWS
        int "Rows per DMA bounce band"
        range 8 60
        default 24
        help
            The PSRAM framebuffer is flushed through two internal-RAM DMA buffers of
            536 x N x 2 bytes each. Larger bands mean fewer SPI transactions but more internal RAM.
            Odd values are rounded down to even (the panel's window needs even start rows).

    config HAIRCLIP_LCD_EN_GPIO
        int "Display enable GPIO (-1 = none)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            GPIO that powers / enables the panel and must be driven high before the panel is reset and
            initialised. -1 (the Waveshare ESP32-S3-AMOLED-1.91 the PixelClip uses) = no such pin.
            LilyGo T-Display-S3 AMOLED V2: 38. The pin is kept driven (also during light sleep).

    config HAIRCLIP_LCD_MADCTL
        hex "MADCTL (0x36) value for the upright landscape picture"
        range 0x00 0xFF
        default 0xF0
        help
            Memory access control written by the init sequence. 0xF0 (MY|MX|MV|ML) is the Waveshare
            board's upright 536x240 landscape. Other boards with the same RM67162 panel may mount it
            differently (LilyGo's own driver uses 0x60 = MX|MV); a 180 degree flip toggles MX|MY (0xC0)
            from this value (display_set_flipped()).
endmenu
